{"review_id": "iclr_SBCMNc3Mq3_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_SBCMNc3Mq3", "passages": [{"quote": "The ECD dataset is a substantial and valuable contribution, offering over 140K PBE-calculated crystal structures and 7147 HSE-calculated structures", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "dataset size and value"}, {"quote": "The paper conducts a comprehensive benchmarking of multiple models, assessing their performance across various tasks and metrics", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental comprehensiveness"}, {"quote": "The paper demonstrates that fine-tuning models trained on PBE data with high-precision HSE data improves predictive accuracy", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodological contribution"}, {"quote": "The description of ECD-HSE-id seems missing in Section 2.5", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of description"}, {"quote": "ChargeE3Net surpasses its invariant counterparts and other non-equivariant models marginally but significantly increases the computation complexity", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "computation-accuracy tradeoff"}, {"quote": "there is minimal analysis of failure cases or instances where the model struggled", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "failure case analysis"}, {"quote": "data augmentation techniques or other methods to improve model generalization are not discussed", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "generalization techniques"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_SBCMNc3Mq3_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_SBCMNc3Mq3", "passages": [{"quote": "The data generated in this work is indeed original", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "originality"}, {"quote": "The functionals PBE and HSE used in this work are indeed the widely accepted ones to compute crystalline inorganic materials", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodological soundness"}, {"quote": "The paper is well-structured, with a clear explanation of the dataset's construction, tasks, and evaluation metrics", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and structure"}, {"quote": "This is a significant contribution to this area. Due to the computational cost to carefully converge the charge densities, it is not easy to generate or to find publicly available data sets", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "significance"}, {"quote": "it would be much better if the authors can keep increasing the number of calculations done with HSE functional", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "high-precision data coverage"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_SBCMNc3Mq3_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_SBCMNc3Mq3", "passages": [{"quote": "The computational efforts used in this study is immense, and the resulting benchmark could be a valuable asset to the ML community", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "computational effort and value"}, {"quote": "Interesting task on predicting the gaps across different functionals", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "task design"}, {"quote": "The work provides minimal justification for predicting electrons instead of the Kohn-Sham Hamiltonian", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological justification"}, {"quote": "There is no comparison with other quantum chemistry benchmarks, like QH9", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "benchmark comparison"}, {"quote": "The EXP-id lacks detail on its 47 entries, which is essential for practical use", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "dataset detail"}, {"quote": "The writing lacks cohesion, with many GPT-like passages", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "Figure 2 is unclear: does moving up or down the ladder imply increased simplicity?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "figure clarity"}, {"quote": "The metrics are limited to MAE for charge density and acceleration ratio. Other measures, such as total energy, HOMO-LUMO gap, electronic spatial extent, or dipole moment, should be included", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "evaluation metrics"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX", "passages": [{"quote": "Authors propose a clear mathematical quantity to compute local complexity of the network", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "mathematical clarity"}, {"quote": "authors describe connections of local complexity of the network to representation learning and its robustness from theoretical viewpoint. Proofs are easy to follow", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical contributions"}, {"quote": "Experimental results with visualization of the proposed complexity measure show that it captures the density of non-linearities", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental validation"}, {"quote": "Authors are also clear with the possible limitations of the connection between metrics", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "limitation discussion"}, {"quote": "there is little discussion on the sharpness of the theoretical bounds", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "bound tightness"}, {"quote": "estimates for $B$ are only given at the initialisation, not after training", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of analysis"}, {"quote": "proof of Theorem 2 essentially directly follows from (Hanin & Rolnick 2019a)", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of proof"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX", "passages": [{"quote": "This study presents a rigorous connection between the geometric characteristics of the ReLU network and adversarial robustness", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical rigor"}, {"quote": "The theoretical analysis links local complexity to the local rank, which relates to the input-space geometry of the ReLU network", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical contribution"}, {"quote": "The analysis of the time evolution of the local complexity and adversarial robustness is limited", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "time evolution analysis"}, {"quote": "The tightness of the bound is not discussed by theory or experiments", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "bound tightness discussion"}, {"quote": "no comprehensive answer to the motivating observation is provided", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of explanation"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX", "passages": [{"quote": "Very well-written and clearly structured paper. The problem has been motivated nicely in the introduction", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing quality and structure"}, {"quote": "The related work section is rigorous and clearly details the current results for this problem", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "related work coverage"}, {"quote": "By linking local complexity to local rank (feature learning), total variation (robustness), and representation cost (parameter optimization), the authors build a solid theoretical foundation", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical foundation"}, {"quote": "they empirically demonstrate such relations by conducting several experiments", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical demonstration"}, {"quote": "there is no direct comparison between local complexity with complexity defined by (Hanin & Rolnick, 2019b) though definitions are quite similar. I think this makes the contribution of this paper incremental", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty and comparison"}, {"quote": "relations between local complexity and others can be loose (i.e., loose inequality)", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "tightness of relationships"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper presents a mathematical foundation for the definitions and claims of local complexity, including theorems and proofs that enhance the credibility of the findings", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "mathematical rigor"}, {"quote": "The links drawn between local complexity, feature learning, and robustness are timely and relevant", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "relevance"}, {"quote": "the empirical results help support the theoretical claims, providing a practical understanding of the phenomena discussed", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical support"}, {"quote": "The definitions of local complexity, local rank, and good neurons, while mathematically interesting, maybe too complex for practical application", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "practical applicability"}, {"quote": "Some sections of the paper are dense and may be challenging for readers unfamiliar with the topic", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "readability"}, {"quote": "the paper could benefit from more extensive empirical experiments to validate the claims", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "empirical validation"}, {"quote": "The paper lacks a thorough discussion of the practical implications of the findings for model design and training", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "practical implications"}]}
{"review_id": "ANCH-2", "paper_id": "ANCH-2", "passages": [{"quote": "This submission provides a rigorous theoretical analysis; the proofs appear correct and the assumptions are clearly stated", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical rigor"}, {"quote": "no code is provided and several hyperparameters are unreported", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "reproducibility"}, {"quote": "The related-work coverage is adequate", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "related work coverage"}, {"quote": "the significance for the broader community seems modest", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "significance"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX_r5", "paper_id": "iclr_IQdlPvj4dX", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper presents a new measure of complexity for functions, connects it to different measures that haven been researched", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty and connections"}, {"quote": "provides directions as to how this measure might shed light on interesting open questions in the field", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "potential impact"}, {"quote": "I would like clarifications as of the significance of the notion of Local Rank. Cited works in the \"Related Works\" section mention roughly similar definitions", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of contribution"}, {"quote": "the empirical experiments provided in the appendix are less than sufficient, and even show a single case of the bound's failure", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "empirical support"}, {"quote": "Please provide more significant empirical evidence for the phenomenon, or a sound proof", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "evidence quality"}, {"quote": "there is only one experiment in the appendix", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental coverage"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_UACXMKAz0Z_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_UACXMKAz0Z", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper proposed an effective technique to improve samplers for diffusion models without introducing extra NFEs, especially in small NFE cases", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "method effectiveness"}, {"quote": "The method can be readily combined with a wide range of existing samplers without post-training the diffusion models", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "method flexibility"}, {"quote": "Extensive experiments were conducted to show the performance of the proposed method. Experiment settings vary across different condition types, sampler orders, guidance strategies, sampling space and datasets", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental comprehensiveness"}, {"quote": "the two types of error are not discriminated in a formal formulation. It is also not clear why the new noise estimation term in eq 10-12 can help reduce the approximation error", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological clarity"}, {"quote": "The connection between the solver and the choice of \\tau is not specified", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological specification"}, {"quote": "The writing of the paper may need improving. The notations in formal formulation of the sampling process can be more consistent. The citation format makes parts of the paper hard to read", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing quality"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_UACXMKAz0Z_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_UACXMKAz0Z", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper's idea is interesting, and the presentation is clear and easy to follow", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and interest"}, {"quote": "Addressing discretization error is a important topic, and this work proposes a novel approach in that direction", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty and importance"}, {"quote": "could the authors clarify what quantity the MSE is measuring and how it directly relates to the discretization error?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of measurement"}, {"quote": "I feel there are other possible interpretations. For example, wouldn't it be possible that as sampling progresses from time T to 1, the discretization error accumulates", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "interpretation completeness"}, {"quote": "It's unclear why only the ε_θ in the second term is evaluated at τ instead of t. Would it be beneficial if both terms were modified similarly?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological justification"}, {"quote": "the formulation of D_{t−1}^ours bears a strong similarity to equation (3) of [1]. Could the authors elaborate on the differences", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "comparison with prior work"}, {"quote": "The numerical results show a very mild improvement over baseline results. In Figures 4 and 5, the proposed method, on average, reduces NFE by no more than one for the same error level", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "improvement magnitude"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_UACXMKAz0Z_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_UACXMKAz0Z", "passages": [{"quote": "The method addresses a highly important issue (approximation error) in DPM sampling which they note is neglecting in prior works", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem importance"}, {"quote": "they demonstrate that this issue may have a greater impact than discretization error. Therefore, this is a highly relevant problem", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem relevance"}, {"quote": "The training-free approach to mitigate approximation error is a good contribution, especially given the fact that this approach can be used in a plug-and-play manner", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "method contribution"}, {"quote": "the authors provide comprehensive experiments in a wide variety of settings and sampling schemes. This demonstrates the robustness of their method", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental robustness"}, {"quote": "Some aspects of the background and method are not very clear. For instance, in equations 8 and 10, are both x_\\theta and \\epsilon_\\theta outputs of the neural network?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of method"}, {"quote": "it should be more clear in the main text how the modified sampling scheme leads to decreased approximation error", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "explanation clarity"}, {"quote": "I think the order of Sections 2.1 and 2.2 is a bit confusing", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "organization"}, {"quote": "The citation style makes it difficult to read the paper, especially the introduction. In-text citations should be surrounded by parentheses", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "citation formatting"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_UACXMKAz0Z_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_UACXMKAz0Z", "passages": [{"quote": "This paper primarily concentrates on reducing the approximation error, a factor overlooked by previous studies", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of focus"}, {"quote": "The experiments conducted in this paper are thorough", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental thoroughness"}, {"quote": "This paper is well composed", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "The paper do not illustrate the computation of the MSE. The analysis of the Dualfast model is based on the probability flow ODE, yet, as per Figure 2, the \"exact form\" is derived from the forward SDE", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological consistency"}, {"quote": "The explanation of diffusion model is incorrect. According to [1], the expression for the optimal \\epsilon_\\theta can be computed explicitly", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "technical correctness"}, {"quote": "The claim $\\epsilon(x_\\tau, \\tau)$ is a better approximation of $\\epsilon(x_t, t)$ can be contradicted with a simple 2D example", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "claim validity"}, {"quote": "only the explicit $\\epsilon_\\theta(x_t, t)$ is replaced with $\\epsilon(x_\\tau, \\tau)$. If $\\epsilon(x_\\tau, \\tau)$ is indeed more accurate, the implicit part in $x_\\theta$ should also be replaced", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological consistency"}, {"quote": "The paper attributes the observed phenomena to a reduction in approximation error without sufficient evidence", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "evidence sufficiency"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_5GuhYMgaap_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_5GuhYMgaap", "passages": [{"quote": "it provides a new way of looking at various ways we interact with LLMs. Using a framework of inductive and deductive reasoning", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novel framework"}, {"quote": "This paper discusses the distinction between inductive and deductive reasoning, and how we may systematically investigate this using a novel framework", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "systematic approach"}, {"quote": "they provide a novel task of their own design. A cypher description task", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "task novelty"}, {"quote": "many available evaluative framework and benchmarks could have already been used in pretraining of many closed LLMs. With an introduction of a novel task, they can robustly test", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "evaluation robustness"}, {"quote": "The framework effectively describes a spectrum between deductive and inductive reasoning", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "framework expressiveness"}, {"quote": "The paper was well written with mostly clear description", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "This framework and subtasks were thoroughly experimented with many current SOTA LLMs", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental coverage"}, {"quote": "The paper does not adequately situate itself with existing literature on reasoning, or discuss the relations between this work with respect to code generation or in-context learning", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "literature positioning"}, {"quote": "The paper and their findings were hard to connect to existing work. I think it would have made the paper stronger to consider how other work in reasoning area compare with this approach", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "connection to prior work"}, {"quote": "The framework relies on a particular case of generation, which is code generation. I think the performances could very much differ in the case of natural language generation", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "generalization concern"}, {"quote": "I believe there were prior work on inductive and deductive reasoning, and some of these prior work does discuss the gap between them. On the claim of novelty, I believe that the question itself is not novel enough", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of question"}, {"quote": "This work does not consider finetuned models, but it would have been interesting to consider them", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "model coverage"}, {"quote": "The writing could be improved in some parts of the paper. I found the deductive part to be a bit lacking in discussion", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "discussion completeness"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_5GuhYMgaap_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_5GuhYMgaap", "passages": [{"quote": "The authors present several contributions to a major research domain in IA: They introduce a notion of several forms of reasoning going on the system, They implement a system to validate their claims. They experimentally obtain unexpected results", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "contributions"}, {"quote": "The paper is also rather easy to follow", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "readability"}, {"quote": "as i read I felt the need for a more formal definition of what is induction and what is deduction", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "formalization"}, {"quote": "I felt I could not understand why statements such as \". By completely disentangling the inductive reasoning of LLMs, our proposed SolverLearner shows the remarkable inductive reasoning capabilities inherent in LLMs.\"", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of claims"}, {"quote": "I would have hoped for a deeper insight into these results. You mention the remarkable induct reasoning of LLMs, but it would be nice (at least for me) to understand how they appear", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "depth of insight"}, {"quote": "Why are the differences so big (Table 13?)", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "explanation of results"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_5GuhYMgaap_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_5GuhYMgaap", "passages": [{"quote": "Disentangling the inductive and deductive capabilities of LLMs seems like an interesting problem", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem interest"}, {"quote": "The types of benchmarks used are varied and several of the state-of-the-art LLMs have been considered in the evaluation", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "benchmark variety"}, {"quote": "The paper seems to suggest that solverlearner is a novel approach, but it is less clear why this is the case. As far I could understand, solver learner just utilizes an external code interpreter", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty clarity"}, {"quote": "I was not clear of the complexity involved to do this, since the approach itself is not described in detail", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological detail"}, {"quote": "The tasks itself also seem to be from prior work (Wu et. Al 2023) apart from the cipher task. Once again, I was not sure if the contribution of the tasks was significantly different from prior work", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "task novelty"}, {"quote": "I was not sure about the leap from observing the experimental results to concluding the "type" of inference the LLM is truly performing internally", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "interpretative validity"}, {"quote": "In terms of the significance of the study, is the fact that deduction is harder than induction significant, i.e., what would be a good application use-case to motivate this study is something that was missing", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "significance and motivation"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_5GuhYMgaap_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_5GuhYMgaap", "passages": [{"quote": "The presentation is clear, fluent, and easy to follow. The task formulation is clear, and the introduction of the proposed framework is transparent", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and presentation"}, {"quote": "The topic of reasoning ability of LLMs is crucial and in need of exploration", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "topic importance"}, {"quote": "The experiments are detailed introduced, with all settings and prompts attached in the appendix", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental detail"}, {"quote": "The task setup does not adequately reflect real-world scenarios. The tasks used in the evaluation, particularly the arithmetic tasks across different number bases and synthetic syntactic tasks, are highly artificial and contrived", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "task realism"}, {"quote": "The proposed SolverLearner, while effective for some inductive tasks, does not generalize well to broader inductive reasoning challenges", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "generalizability"}, {"quote": "The paper fails to adequately compare its results with alternative approaches to reasoning in LLMs, such as chain-of-thought prompting, least-to-most prompting", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "comparison with baselines"}, {"quote": "The scope of deductive evaluation is too narrow. The deductive reasoning tasks primarily focus on counterfactual arithmetic (e.g., base-9 vs. base-10 arithmetic), which is a very specific case", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "evaluation scope"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_27SSnLl85x_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_27SSnLl85x", "passages": [{"quote": "I find the paper clearly writtin and well presented, the authors make an effort presenting the dense results in a clear manner", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and presentation"}, {"quote": "The authors, to the best of my understanding, extend the theory around GDLNs and allow for a more in-depth study of the training dynamics of ReLU networks", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical contribution"}, {"quote": "I find the exposition of quite toyish tasks enlightning and make the paper more easy to follow", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "pedagogical value"}, {"quote": "I can not judge fairly the novely of the paper, especially its relation to Saxe et a., 2022. For me, it would have been helpful to highlight the novelty a bit more", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty clarity"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_27SSnLl85x_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_27SSnLl85x", "passages": [{"quote": "The introduction of ReLN as a GDLN variant to study ReLU dynamics is innovative and offers a new angle on understanding feature learning in finite ReLU networks", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of approach"}, {"quote": "The paper provides theoretical insights into inductive biases in ReLU networks, particularly regarding structured mixed selectivity and node reuse", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical insights"}, {"quote": "It remains unclear why ReLU's training dynamics and mixed selectivity properties cannot be derived directly from ReLU networks, as they're already nonlinear", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological justification"}, {"quote": "The approach is demonstrated on relatively simple tasks, raising concerns about scalability. For instance, applying ReLNs to realistic datasets like MNIST remains unaddressed", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scalability concerns"}, {"quote": "Terms like \"feature learning\" and \"pathway doing feature learning\" (line 302) lack precise definitions", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "definitional clarity"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_27SSnLl85x_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_27SSnLl85x", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper presents a novel framework Rectified Linear Network to analytically investigate the dynamic of finite-width single-hidden layer neural networks", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "framework novelty"}, {"quote": "The paper provides theoretical proof for the equivalence between ReLN and ReLU for the case of finite-width single-hidden layer network and verified that the predicted loss matches with the empirical loss", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical validation"}, {"quote": "The paper clearly present the background relevant work, including the formulation of Gated Deep Linear Network, decomposition of eigenmodes, and derived of learning dynamic", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of background"}, {"quote": "The theoretical proofs are presented clearly with both informal and formal versions, along with a proof sketch in the main paper, and a detailed proof in the appendix", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "proof presentation"}, {"quote": "The empirical results (including the dataset and figures) are clearly presented with clear figure and caption, along with descriptions in the main text", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical presentation"}, {"quote": "The main theoretical results of the paper requires very strong assumptions (L159, *Assumption 2.1*) in both (1) input dataset (*The dataset correlation matrices are mutually diagonalizable*) and (2) model training trajectory", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "restrictiveness of assumptions"}, {"quote": "the authors did not offer any analysis on specific scenario in which these assumption holds or not hold", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "assumption analysis"}, {"quote": "The empirical experiments that supports the claim and theoretical results only includes single-layer hidden network on a simple synthetic dataset", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "limited experimental scope"}, {"quote": "it would be helpful and more convincing if the authors can demonstrate that the proposed approach work in a realistic image dataset (MNIST, CIFAR, etc.) with a more realistic and variety of model architectures", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "real dataset evaluation"}, {"quote": "it's unclear whether this clustering algorithms can scale with realistic dataset and larger models", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scalability of method"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_27SSnLl85x_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_27SSnLl85x", "passages": [{"quote": "The approach of identifying the linear submodules learned by ReLU networks and using this for tractability of the analysis is interesting", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "analytical approach"}, {"quote": "natural modules to learn the structure in the data are exactly recovered by ReLU networks together with the learning speed. This provides mechanistic understanding", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "mechanistic insights"}, {"quote": "While this is a nice and tractable toy model for the learning dynamics of 2-layer ReLU networks, generalizability of the findings is questionable", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "generalizability"}, {"quote": "The results only hold for the synthetic and very specific structure considered. The relevance on real data sets or practical architectures remains elusive, as it is not evaluated", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "practical relevance"}, {"quote": "The authors show and acknowledge that the silent alignment Assumption 2 already does not hold for 2-hidden-layer ReLU nets", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "assumption violation"}, {"quote": "In Figure 6, against the authors' claim of 'sharing the same characteristics', ReLU networks appear to make larger, sharper steps in the loss", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "claim inconsistency"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_Gd6QrBLHBN_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_Gd6QrBLHBN", "passages": [{"quote": "The work is well presented, and easy to follow", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "presentation quality"}, {"quote": "The experiments do show that the introduction of an altar does reduce the cognitive burden on agents while addressing cooperation challenges and promote normative social order", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental validation"}, {"quote": "performance is increased compared to simply having a hidden rule/norm built into the reward of the sanctioning actions", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "performance improvement"}, {"quote": "The experiments are solid and show the improvement achieved by the introduction of altars", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental solidity"}, {"quote": "These institutions/altars have to know the environment rules to dynamically change. I am not convinced we always have that knowledge available", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "practical feasibility"}, {"quote": "We won't always be able to alter an environment to include an altar, how do we address such situations?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "generalizability"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_Gd6QrBLHBN_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_Gd6QrBLHBN", "passages": [{"quote": "The idea is novel and deals with an interesting problem in multi-agent AI research", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty and problem interest"}, {"quote": "Results show that indeed altared environments promote collaboration and resilience in agents", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "results"}, {"quote": "Poorly written and difficult to read", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "There are many grammatical errors that lead to ambiguity and ruin the flow of the text", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "grammatical quality"}, {"quote": "Paragraphs are long and packed with multiple ideas making them hard to read", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "paragraph structure"}, {"quote": "following the link provided in the abstract leads to an empty repository", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "code availability"}, {"quote": "The authors make claims and mentions models that are not explained nor cited", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "citation completeness"}, {"quote": "The contribution of this work is can be boiled down to adding manually programmed indications of social rules explicitly into the agents' observations. This is done with no theoretical justification and relatively weak intuition", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "contribution significance"}, {"quote": "Figure 1, is not clear at all and does not help demonstrate the differences between the versions of Markov games", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "figure clarity"}, {"quote": "Environment description in main paper is insufficient", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "environment description"}, {"quote": "showcases only harvest domains. There are other social dilemma domains like cleanup, economist, prisoners dilemma, etc.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "domain coverage"}, {"quote": "There is inconsistent plot coloring and labeling of plots, making it difficult to follow the results", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "plot consistency"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_Gd6QrBLHBN_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_Gd6QrBLHBN", "passages": [{"quote": "Cooperative alignment in multi-agent systems, the problem this paper aims to tackle, is highly relevant and important", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem importance"}, {"quote": "The idea is good. Classification institutions for normative alignment make intuitive sense and are well-grounded in social science and anthropology", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "idea quality"}, {"quote": "The introduction is very well written", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "introduction quality"}, {"quote": "To me, Figure 1 is not very informative. This figure should provide a clear and unambiguous overview of your approach for the busy reader. The caption is just \"Overview of the Altared Framework\"", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "figure informativeness"}, {"quote": "Section 3 does not flow well and feels confused. There is very low information density per word here", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "section organization"}, {"quote": "Weak results. This is my primary concern and biggest reason I'm going to recommend rejection. These results are far from convincing", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "results strength"}, {"quote": "It looks to me like there is no difference at all in mean episode reward for allelopathic harvest, and three seeds is not enough for a rigorous evaluation", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "statistical rigor"}, {"quote": "the error bands seem to abruptly shrink twice on your Commons Harvest mean episode reward plot, with no variance at all at the end; this looks a lot like the three seeds ran were not all run to termination", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental completeness"}, {"quote": "No ethics section? Who gets to decide the norms that the institution classifies as \"right\"?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "ethics discussion"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_Gd6QrBLHBN_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_Gd6QrBLHBN", "passages": [{"quote": "Well-written paper, reads naturally (flow, language)", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "Introduction and Preliminaries set the stage very well and explain the broader interest in the problems touched", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem framing"}, {"quote": "Experiments and their results do not support the claims made by unfair comparison. For example, we compare mean rewards while one of the baselines has a clear disadvantage in earning rewards", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental fairness"}, {"quote": "Code is not accessible to reproduce or investigate the work further", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "reproducibility"}, {"quote": "No description on how the altar \"dynamic\" attribute works", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological detail"}, {"quote": "No mention of the results of the original authors of the Melting Pot environment suite", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "baseline comparison"}, {"quote": "The abstract is very ambiguous, assuming specific knowledge of the environments, which can confuse readers who are not knowledgeable", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "abstract clarity"}, {"quote": "Figure captions are insufficient for most / all figures in the main body of the paper", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "figure captions"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_7BLXhmWvwF_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_7BLXhmWvwF", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is well-written and presents its ideas clearly with solid formulation", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing clarity"}, {"quote": "The proposed approach of modeling robotic manipulation problems as heterogeneous graph learning problems is well-motivated and clever to unify the structure", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "approach motivation"}, {"quote": "The adaptation of *SE(3)* equivariant message passing networks is reasonable and suitable to exploit the geometric symmetry", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodological suitability"}, {"quote": "HEPi is one of the first studies of equivariant policies on 3D space within a reinforcement learning setting for robotic manipulation", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "The empirical experiments are comprehensive and sound to support the arguments. Most results are averaged over 10 seeds using interquartile mean with 95% confidence intervals, which is also statistically robust", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "statistical rigor"}, {"quote": "The experiments are limited to simple geometric shapes like ropes, triangles, and stars, which can be easily modeled using a few nodes (< 100 in all the experiments)", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental scope"}, {"quote": "I doubt whether HEPi can still generalize to all those complicated geometries, which brings much computational complexity to graph learning", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scalability concern"}, {"quote": "The current framework assumes that the object coordinates are readily available in the observation, which is basically a simulation setting", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "real-world applicability"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_7BLXhmWvwF_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_7BLXhmWvwF", "passages": [{"quote": "Clever Design: This paper includes several ingenious designs. The use of EMPNs The use of SE(3)-equivariant networks ensures that the model naturally possesses SE(3) generalization", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "design quality"}, {"quote": "the introduction of TRPL in place of traditional PPO makes hyperparameter tuning easier, addressing a significant challenge in RL training", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodological contribution"}, {"quote": "One of the major issues in RL is poor reproducibility. However, in this paper, the authors provide a detailed appendix that lists experimental information, including the reward function and hyperparameters", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "reproducibility"}, {"quote": "This paper provides a detailed demonstration of the proposed benchmark tasks in the video and clearly defines these tasks in the appendix", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "benchmark clarity"}, {"quote": "this paper uses ground-truth model inputs and does not incorporate a physical robot, which means it cannot be directly applied to real-world scenarios", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "real-world application"}, {"quote": "This paper does not seem to have any special designs focused on geometry, although graphs do play a role", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "geometry-aware design"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_7BLXhmWvwF_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_7BLXhmWvwF", "passages": [{"quote": "The proposed heterogeneous graph representation is a general representation for both rigid and deformable object manipulation tasks, and captures the geometric structure of the object", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "representation generality"}, {"quote": "HEPi is a novel formulation of graph-based equivariant policy build on top of the heterogeneous graph representation that enables rl for manipulation of diverse shapes", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "policy novelty"}, {"quote": "The paper has demonstrated thorough evaluations and ablations in simulation, with convincing results proving that the proposed method has better performance, sample-efficiency, and generalizability", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "evaluation thoroughness"}, {"quote": "Detailed discussions are provided for the results, providing interesting insights", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "discussion quality"}, {"quote": "The object model that contains vertices are required for the object node representation, which is the main observation for the policy. This might not be easy to get in the real world", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "observation requirement"}, {"quote": "The paper demonstrates thorough evaluations across various simulation benchmarks, but lacks real-world evaluations to make the method fully convincing", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "real-world validation"}]}
{"review_id": "ANCH-1", "paper_id": "ANCH-1", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper tackles an interesting problem", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem interest"}, {"quote": "the experimental evaluation is thorough, covering five datasets with proper ablations", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental thoroughness"}, {"quote": "the novelty is limited: the proposed method is a straightforward combination of two existing techniques", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "The writing is also difficult to follow in Sections 3-4, with undefined notation", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing clarity"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_7BLXhmWvwF_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_7BLXhmWvwF", "passages": [{"quote": "I find the story in this paper intuitive and convincing. While the two core building blocks (heterogeneous graphs and equivariant policies) have been explored in prior arts, this paper presents a proper combination", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "combination quality"}, {"quote": "I feel the proposed method has the potential to be extended to manipulate fluid and rigid/soft/fluid-coupled systems", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "extensibility"}, {"quote": "the benchmark scenes are still relatively simple because the setup only models a point-like end effector, ignoring kinematic and dynamic constraints in practical robotic hand/arm structures", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "benchmark realism"}, {"quote": "From a dynamic perspective, the 2D rigid-sliding task is too trivial to be a valuable benchmark for evaluating this paper and its baselines", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "task complexity"}, {"quote": "Deformable objects can be classified by their dimensions: codimension-2 (e.g., ropes), codimension-1 (e.g., cloths), and codimension-0 (e.g., rubber balls). The paper seems to consider the first two categories only", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "deformable object coverage"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_G19piTjVYA_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_G19piTjVYA", "passages": [{"quote": "I find the idea of regularizing based on topological ordering very interesting, especially because this can cause many downstream errors", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "idea interest"}, {"quote": "Using a differentiable version of Intersort as a regularizer seems a fitting and effective way to realize this idea", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "method appropriateness"}, {"quote": "It is also clever to derive a score function which uses learned causal orders to avoid acyclicity constraints", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "technical cleverness"}, {"quote": "Empirically and theoretically, the results of DiffIntersort seem close to Intersort, which is reassuring for the differentiable relaxation", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "validation quality"}, {"quote": "I find the novelty in Intersort -> DiffIntersort somewhat limited; I recognize the use of a potential is nontrivial, but this is still mostly just combining Chevalley et al. (2024) and Annadani et al. (2023) in a straightforward way", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "it doesn't seem like there is code available for CausalDisco, or for the experiments included in the paper", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "code availability"}, {"quote": "the details in the manuscript regarding CausalDisco are somewhat sparse (e.g.., hyperparmeters used for regaularization)", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological detail"}, {"quote": "I have doubts about the presentation of \"CausalDisco with constraint.\" A constraint only appears in Eq. (8), and it is likely more appropriate to present as a bilevel optimization problem", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "presentation of constraint"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_G19piTjVYA_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_G19piTjVYA", "passages": [{"quote": "The experimental results is relatively comprehensive", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental coverage"}, {"quote": "The introduction of differentiable operator is novel to me and may be beneficial to other permutation based methods", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of operator"}, {"quote": "The motivation of the work is unclear: What is being discovered? In section 3.3 the authors say \"Our goal is to recover the causal structure and ordering of the variables from both observational and interventional data\", but in the title and elsewhere just the causal ordering is emphasized", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of objective"}, {"quote": "I doubt that the causal ordering learning in this setting is not a necessary problem", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "problem necessity"}, {"quote": "What are exactly all the assumptions needed in this work? I only see Interventional Faithfulness. Does it mean that this work, together with the score used and the distance function used, is fully nonparametric?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "assumption clarity"}, {"quote": "For the identifiability of the causal order itself, what is needed? The authors says they \"derive the causal order of the variables when many single-variable interventions are available\", but how `many' is many?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "identifiability conditions"}, {"quote": "The presentation can be improved. E.g., the definition 2 (top order divergence) serves only as a metric of evaluation, and should not be put at the beginning of the method part", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "presentation structure"}, {"quote": "More detailed literature review on causal discovery from interventional data, and on the differentiable ordering learning is expected", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "literature review"}]}
